 No. 2 Bulldogs. Blake Berlowitz again got the start.","published":"2026-10-03T19:59:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50090244/sources-vanderbilt-qb-jared-curtis-attempt-play-vs-georgia","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 recruit AJ Randle Jr. flips from Miami to Notre Dame","description":"Notre Dame coach Marcus Freeman flipped Miami pledge AJ Randle Jr., ESPN's No. 9 outside linebacker in the 2027 recruiting class, to fill a late-cycle need.","published":"2026-11-22T21:22:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50565158/2027-recruit-aj-randle-jr-flips-miami-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pac-12 reveals unique flex schedule for season's final week","description":"The Pac-12 announced its unique flex schedule for the final week of the regular season early Sunday morning.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564960/pac-12-reveals-unique-flex-schedule-season-final-week","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Montana State ranked No. 1, 5-7 LIU makes FCS bracket as conference champ","description":"Defending national champion Montana State received the top seed for the 24-team FCS playoffs, while Northeast Conference champion LIU (5-7) became the first playoff team with a losing record since 2017.","published":"2026-11-22T21:06:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564910/montana-state-grabs-top-seed-24-team-fcs-playoff-bracket","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest rewards DC Scottie Hazelton with contract extension","description":"Wake Forest defensive coordinator Scottie Hazelton has signed a contract extension.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564902/wake-forest-rewards-dc-scottie-hazelton-extension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-22T20:32:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who are the candidates and what are the priorities after TCU fired Sonny Dykes?","description":"Things started well for Dykes, but now the Horned Frogs are looking for a new coach and should have options.","published":"2026-11-22T19:55:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50323301/tcu-candidates-personnel-recruits","type":"Story","byline":"Eli Lederman, Max Olson and Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios for Week 12?","description":"Here's what teams from every conference would need to play for their league championship.","published":"2026-11-22T19:15:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512475/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5084047/nate-frazier","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nate_Frazier"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Nate Frazier","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nate_Frazier","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:22Z","intro":"Nathaniel Frazier Jr. (born September 26, 2005) is an American college football running back for the Georgia Bulldogs of the Southeastern Conference (SEC).","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Frazier attended Mater Dei High School in Santa Ana, California. At the conclusion of his senior year, he was selected to the All-American Bowl. One of the top running back recruits in the country, Frazier committed to play college football at the University of Georgia, over offers from Alabama, Oregon, and Texas A&M."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In Frazier's collegiate debut against Clemson, he rushed for 83 yards and a touchdown on 11 carries. Against UMass, he rushed for 136 yards and three touchdowns in a 59–21 victory. Against Georgia Tech, Frazier scored the game winning two-point conversion run to secure a 44–42 victory after eight overtimes. He finished his true freshman season rushing for 671 yards and eight touchdowns."}]}}